WEBVTT

00:12.630 --> 00:14.530
It's totally inedible!

00:14.530 --> 00:16.930
Why do I have to go through something like this?

00:16.930 --> 00:18.870
That damn Raichou...

00:18.870 --> 00:20.910
There's no use complaining now.

00:21.130 --> 00:25.100
If you're picky, your body won't move at a critical time when it needs to.

00:25.100 --> 00:27.420
You're really tough.

00:28.140 --> 00:30.870
S-S-S-Shiruku!

00:30.870 --> 00:31.890
Behind you!

00:31.890 --> 00:32.620
Behind me?

02:00.720 --> 02:03.680
Tsundere, kuudere, yandere. They're all ancient relics now.

02:03.680 --> 02:04.990
The ultimate and the invincible genre:

02:04.990 --> 02:06.100
That'd be goddere.

02:06.100 --> 02:09.310
It's not like I'm being omnipotent and omniscient for your sake.

02:48.870 --> 02:52.040
This is all because Ouka-kun's family didn't do their job.

02:52.960 --> 02:56.970
I think it was because you didn't give them a proper explanation.

02:56.970 --> 02:58.670
I guess I don't have a choice.

03:00.090 --> 03:02.990
Emergency defense mode.

03:35.180 --> 03:39.440
The monster eggs that have been dropping since yesterday are still falling to the Earth heavily,

03:39.440 --> 03:41.930
and one after another, are hatching, attacking-

03:44.030 --> 03:45.200
Everyone hurry.

03:45.200 --> 03:48.660
Teika, you take Yuuka and everyone else
and hurry to the evacuation facility.

03:48.660 --> 03:49.800
I will.

03:49.800 --> 03:51.480
Oh no, what should I do?

03:51.480 --> 03:53.040
This is the expected doom?

03:53.310 --> 03:56.170
Is it related to the Gouyokuou guy that Raichou mentioned?

03:56.660 --> 03:57.790
Probably.

03:57.790 --> 04:01.680
But for now, let's split up and evacuate as many people as possible.

04:01.680 --> 04:03.550
We simply have a problem, Dad!

04:03.550 --> 04:04.890
Gekka's missing.

04:04.890 --> 04:06.130
What?

04:06.700 --> 04:07.830
What is she...

04:07.830 --> 04:08.770
You're right.

04:08.770 --> 04:10.380
What'll we do, Father?

04:12.020 --> 04:13.790
We don't have any time to lose.

04:13.790 --> 04:14.320
Let's go!

04:14.320 --> 04:15.600
Don't worry!

04:15.600 --> 04:18.030
Gekka can take care most stuff by herself!

04:19.650 --> 04:21.220
Keep it up, Yuuka-chan!

04:21.220 --> 04:21.920
Yup!

04:31.830 --> 04:33.990
What ugly monsters you guys are.

04:33.990 --> 04:37.250
You guys think you had a chance against the god?!

04:37.250 --> 04:38.380
Everyone, that way!

04:38.380 --> 04:39.210
Please calm down!

04:45.870 --> 04:48.240
Where could Gekka have gone?

05:00.140 --> 05:01.290
I don't get it...

05:02.040 --> 05:04.780
What is this emotion I'm feeling?

05:05.390 --> 05:06.460
I...

05:06.990 --> 05:08.160
I...

05:12.510 --> 05:14.330
I want to see Ouka.

05:19.200 --> 05:22.660
Would you be me?

05:26.720 --> 05:28.680
Gosh, one right after another.

05:28.680 --> 05:30.100
Are you all right, Kyouka?

05:30.100 --> 05:31.140
I'm sick of this!

05:31.140 --> 05:34.820
There's no end to this if we don't find Gouyokuou and beat him.

05:34.820 --> 05:37.810
But we don't know where Gouyokuou is.

05:38.250 --> 05:41.060
I doubt he'll pop up that conveniently.

05:47.300 --> 05:48.540
Um...

05:48.540 --> 05:49.870
Could this be...

06:20.030 --> 06:21.110
I am...

06:22.400 --> 06:23.400
...an alie-

06:26.010 --> 06:27.020
Kyouka!

06:27.020 --> 06:29.290
No matter how suspicious one might be,
you mustn't punch them without warning!

06:29.290 --> 06:31.320
He was overly fishy, so I couldn't stop my impulse.

06:34.140 --> 06:36.000
Excuse me, dear Earthling.

06:36.000 --> 06:41.360
I was taught that was custom for aliens landing on Earth.

06:41.360 --> 06:45.460
I am an alien, after all, who doesn't know anything around here, so please forgive me.

06:46.150 --> 06:48.140
Here's my card.

06:48.140 --> 06:49.230
Thank you very much.

06:49.230 --> 06:50.490
One for you, too.

06:50.490 --> 06:51.060
Yeah.

06:51.060 --> 06:52.410
Let's see...

06:52.410 --> 06:55.150
Here, please have one.

06:55.150 --> 06:57.500
Hello.

06:57.500 --> 06:58.950
There we go.

06:58.950 --> 06:59.560
Here.

06:59.560 --> 07:00.430
Here.

07:00.950 --> 07:02.280
Excuse me.

07:03.130 --> 07:04.700
Yes, how can I help you?

07:04.700 --> 07:08.910
You have to write your name and address on your business card.

07:08.910 --> 07:12.710
Ah, I see. So that's how business cards work.

07:12.710 --> 07:15.990
I'm not used to the concept of a written language, so it didn't cross my mind.

07:15.990 --> 07:17.810
Thank you so much for pointing that out.

07:20.600 --> 07:21.920
May I take those back please.

07:21.920 --> 07:22.830
May I?

07:23.000 --> 07:24.150
May I?

07:26.780 --> 07:27.300
All right.

07:29.010 --> 07:31.800
If I may properly introduce myself.

07:33.440 --> 07:35.300
My name is Gouyokuou.

07:35.300 --> 07:36.270
So you were.

07:36.270 --> 07:37.290
My address is outer space.

07:37.290 --> 07:37.970
That's way too vague!

07:37.970 --> 07:39.970
And you're not explaining anything!

07:39.970 --> 07:41.490
Did I make a mistake?

07:41.490 --> 07:42.760
No, nothing's wrong, but...

07:42.760 --> 07:43.930
I hate beating around the bush!

07:43.930 --> 07:46.670
You! Let me ask you a question straight up!

07:46.670 --> 07:49.290
Are you a danger to this Earth?!

07:49.290 --> 07:49.780
Danger?

07:49.930 --> 07:56.210
Yes. If you are here with the intention of bringing disaster to Earth, then we can't welcome you.

07:56.210 --> 07:57.910
Not like I need to hear your answer.

07:57.910 --> 08:00.700
A strange creature like you has to be an enemy!

08:01.810 --> 08:04.040
What to say...

08:04.570 --> 08:09.830
I get the feeling that people on this planet hold a negative connotation with the word "alien".

08:09.830 --> 08:12.610
Sad. How very sad!

08:13.440 --> 08:16.070
Why can't we understand each other?!

08:16.070 --> 08:17.850
Just because I'm an alien!

08:17.850 --> 08:19.930
Just because we look different!

08:20.170 --> 08:23.310
Why must we stand against each other like enemies?

08:23.310 --> 08:26.400
If you're going to say that it's my destiny, then I curse my destiny!

08:25.680 --> 08:26.400
You're too close...

08:26.400 --> 08:29.730
I hate myself for making you guys not believe and alarmed at me!

08:26.400 --> 08:28.900
Get off, I said.

08:29.960 --> 08:31.570
Stupid me! Stupid me! Stupid me!

08:32.370 --> 08:33.810
You didn't have to punch that hard.

08:33.810 --> 08:35.540
But I won't fall into despair!

08:35.540 --> 08:40.870
The way to achieve a better future is always within our grasp!

08:40.870 --> 08:44.290
Rather than that, would you answer the question?

08:44.700 --> 08:48.000
Don't you already know what my answer is?

08:49.200 --> 08:51.000
I have no intention of bringing conflict.

08:51.000 --> 08:55.130
I don't plan on invading this planet, nor do I plan on hurting anyone.

08:55.800 --> 08:58.660
Since I... I...

08:59.470 --> 09:01.970
I came to this planet to fall in love.

09:02.800 --> 09:04.730
Love, he says?

09:05.580 --> 09:06.230
Yup.

09:06.230 --> 09:11.410
I've had enough! I will beat him up and put an end to this stupid mess!

09:09.950 --> 09:11.420
You mustn't!

09:11.410 --> 09:15.920
Don't stop me, Ouka! There's no way they're not connected!

09:11.830 --> 09:14.740
So those monsters that are born from those eggs have nothing to do with you?

09:15.920 --> 09:18.220
Screw him with the "yup". Think of your size!

09:17.530 --> 09:19.020
They're not totally unrelated.

09:18.220 --> 09:19.860
I need to smack him!

09:19.140 --> 09:20.830
Since they're part of my body.

09:19.860 --> 09:20.830
Let me punch him!

09:21.000 --> 09:21.790
Huh?

09:21.790 --> 09:24.960
If I were to make an analogy, they're like white blood cells and red blood cells.

09:25.420 --> 09:29.670
They deliver the nutrition they gather from other organisms to me.

09:29.670 --> 09:32.470
I'm made so that's the only way for me to get energy.

09:32.960 --> 09:36.470
Whenever I go to a new planet,
I first dispatch a whole lot of them and-

09:36.470 --> 09:38.090
Cut your crap!

09:38.470 --> 09:40.430
What was that for, Earthling?!

09:40.430 --> 09:44.540
Them moving around is a survival process and is completely separate to my will.

09:44.540 --> 09:45.350
I have no ill intentions.

09:45.350 --> 09:47.490
That's what's worse! You're a big bother!

09:47.490 --> 09:50.860
I don't care if it's love or not!
Call them all back and get off of Earth!

09:51.910 --> 09:57.700
Fine. If you don't like a part of my body,
then I will take responsibility and obliterate them.

09:58.320 --> 10:01.820
But I can't just turn back around to space.

10:01.820 --> 10:05.100
After all, I haven't met my beloved yet.

10:05.100 --> 10:05.960
You still dare say things like that?!

10:05.960 --> 10:07.370
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

10:30.000 --> 10:31.360
This is...

10:35.940 --> 10:37.600
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

10:38.500 --> 10:40.710
It looks like I'm just too strong.

10:40.710 --> 10:48.270
If I don't restrain myself with these concealing poles, purely my presence, motions, or voice could even destroy a planet.

10:48.270 --> 10:49.640
What?!

10:49.640 --> 10:52.170
Then if we were to attack him carelessly...

11:05.140 --> 11:06.560
No!!!

11:06.730 --> 11:10.340
Because of this strength, I'm going to be misunderstood by everyone again!

11:10.340 --> 11:13.090
If I released my entire strength by mistake,

11:13.400 --> 11:17.920
I would end up destroying everything on this world without any problem!

11:18.150 --> 11:22.910
But really, I simply came to this world following my beloved.

11:22.910 --> 11:25.930
So please. Just leave me alone.

11:29.330 --> 11:31.170
Unbelievable.

11:31.170 --> 11:32.820
He's dangerous.

11:32.820 --> 11:36.760
His existence jeopardizes the Earth's future.

11:40.610 --> 11:42.810
What a troublemaker.

11:42.810 --> 11:44.210
Either way...

11:47.680 --> 11:51.330
It seems I must go put an end to this.

11:51.330 --> 11:52.690
Hey, is that Gekka?

11:53.270 --> 11:54.380
Is that you, Gekka?

11:54.380 --> 11:56.070
Oh, Hyouka.

11:56.280 --> 11:58.780
You recognize me as me?

11:58.780 --> 12:02.190
Your sensors are a little too sensitive.

12:02.190 --> 12:03.320
What are you talking about?

12:03.900 --> 12:05.370
Just talking to myself.

12:05.990 --> 12:08.780
Hyouka. You're a strong boy.

12:08.780 --> 12:10.920
Be sure to protect everyone.

12:10.920 --> 12:13.960
What are you talking about, Gekka? You're not making sense.

12:13.960 --> 12:16.770
This is all my fault.

12:16.770 --> 12:18.070
I'm sorry.

12:18.070 --> 12:20.540
If something happened, then talk to me.

12:20.540 --> 12:22.570
I might be able to help you.

12:22.570 --> 12:23.990
We're a family, right?

12:24.410 --> 12:26.470
I'm responsible for this.

12:26.470 --> 12:28.970
So I must put an end to this.

12:28.970 --> 12:32.230
Don't trouble me too much.

12:47.660 --> 12:49.370
Why, Gekka?

12:51.450 --> 12:52.520
What's that?!

12:52.520 --> 12:53.420
A peach?!

13:06.580 --> 13:10.720
A drink after work sure tastes good.

13:11.520 --> 13:13.980
What's your work, sir?

13:14.160 --> 13:16.380
Oh, I'm sorry for the late introduction.

13:16.380 --> 13:18.110
Here's my card.

13:18.920 --> 13:22.270
Manager of Space, Gouyokuou-san.

13:23.040 --> 13:26.360
Wow! You were a king?

13:26.360 --> 13:29.280
No, it's nothing that extravagant.

13:29.970 --> 13:33.470
A king who can't make the girl he loves look at him is...

13:35.810 --> 13:37.320
Love is hard.

13:37.320 --> 13:39.500
You're in love, sir?

13:39.500 --> 13:40.380
Yeah.

13:40.380 --> 13:43.460
I hear there's a saying on Earth, "to wait patiently,"

13:44.010 --> 13:48.380
but I've waited and thought only of her for a thousand years.

13:48.380 --> 13:50.860
It's only a split-second in my life.

13:50.860 --> 13:55.650
But every second... every minute felt so long.

13:56.200 --> 13:57.480
A thousand years...

13:57.480 --> 13:59.760
I don't really get it, but I understand your feelings!

13:59.760 --> 14:02.160
You're a romanticist!

14:02.610 --> 14:04.090
You can tell, cat-girl?

14:04.510 --> 14:07.300
All right! We shall talk the night away!

14:07.300 --> 14:08.990
Yes! A toast to us!

14:08.990 --> 14:10.240
Cheers!

14:12.380 --> 14:14.580
Sir! Your drink got on you!

14:15.450 --> 14:17.650
I just realized an important fact!

14:17.650 --> 14:19.030
I don't have a mouth!

14:19.030 --> 14:20.980
And without mouth, I can't drink!

14:21.590 --> 14:24.080
What an oversight!

14:24.080 --> 14:26.640
It's a perfect crime that deceived all the police!

14:26.640 --> 14:27.550
Really?!

14:31.610 --> 14:34.480
Why do we get so many strange customers?

14:34.480 --> 14:36.660
Shut up and keep mixing.

14:53.290 --> 14:56.430
Sir. Please park your vehicle in the parking lot behind the building.

14:56.430 --> 14:57.950
It's not mine.

14:59.720 --> 15:02.170
You seem to be having quite a bit of fun.

15:07.890 --> 15:09.180
This voice!

15:09.180 --> 15:11.580
Ge-Ge-Ge-Ge-Ge-Ge-

15:11.580 --> 15:14.220
Gegege no ge? What are you talking about.

15:14.220 --> 15:16.410
Long time no see, Gouyokuou.

15:16.410 --> 15:17.240
Gekka?!

15:17.240 --> 15:18.960
What do I do? What do I do?

15:21.410 --> 15:22.270
I missed you.

15:22.740 --> 15:25.490
I never did.

15:25.490 --> 15:30.030
But here I came, thinking I'd thank you for keeping the promise, and...

15:30.190 --> 15:34.680
I find you drinking with a girl next to you, having too much fun?

15:40.250 --> 15:41.120
It's here!

15:41.120 --> 15:42.390
What is it this time?

15:42.390 --> 15:44.110
You've got it wrong! It's not what you think!

15:42.390 --> 15:45.630
You go ahead and keep enjoying your time with her!

15:44.110 --> 15:45.630
PLACEHOLDER

15:45.630 --> 15:46.050
PLACEHOLDER

15:45.630 --> 15:47.770
Let go! Let go!

15:46.050 --> 15:49.580
Why? Why? Have I done anything wrong?

15:49.580 --> 15:50.930
Please, calm your temper.

15:50.460 --> 15:51.960
God, you're annoying!

15:50.930 --> 15:53.210
Gekka, my adorable girl!

15:51.960 --> 15:53.670
Get your hands off of me, you filthy animal!

15:53.790 --> 15:55.070
Gekka!

15:55.070 --> 15:55.860
Gekka?!

15:55.860 --> 15:57.720
Father. Mother.

15:57.720 --> 15:58.470
Gekka?!

15:58.700 --> 16:00.690
Are you really Gekka?

16:02.040 --> 16:04.060
This is getting more complicated.

16:07.820 --> 16:11.030
It was a thousand years ago.

16:11.030 --> 16:14.010
I was a god of a certain planet.

16:14.010 --> 16:20.390
However, the only thing that existed there were Aquaticians born from my body.

16:20.390 --> 16:25.710
I spent a lonely life, day after day.

16:25.710 --> 16:26.890
That's when...

16:26.890 --> 16:28.020
Hi.

16:29.240 --> 16:30.840
Are you alone, too?

16:37.080 --> 16:37.850
Who are you?

16:38.130 --> 16:40.110
My name is Gouyokuou.

16:40.110 --> 16:40.850
What about you?

16:41.290 --> 16:42.490
I'm...

16:43.210 --> 16:45.250
I don't have a name.

16:45.250 --> 16:47.110
I never needed one.

16:47.780 --> 16:50.080
What business do you have on this planet?

16:50.080 --> 16:52.270
Do you seek my treasure?

16:52.270 --> 16:53.270
Treasure?

16:53.790 --> 16:56.820
Rather than a treasure... let's see...

16:57.540 --> 16:59.200
I would like to have you.

17:01.610 --> 17:02.580
That's impossible.

17:03.460 --> 17:05.510
I'm scared of you.

17:05.510 --> 17:07.690
I do not wish to be with you.

17:10.040 --> 17:12.120
So your name is Gekka?

17:12.120 --> 17:13.280
Gekka...

17:13.660 --> 17:14.890
Gekka.

17:14.890 --> 17:15.840
Gekka!

17:16.060 --> 17:18.530
I clearly turned him down.

17:18.530 --> 17:22.240
Yet he kept visiting me every day.

17:22.240 --> 17:25.430
But you finally did promise with me in the end!

17:25.430 --> 17:27.470
That you'd give me an answer if I waited for a thousand years.

17:27.470 --> 17:33.490
So he did. He kept the promise and waited for me for a thousand years...

17:33.490 --> 17:37.980
...while, in my stead, protecting the planet I left.

17:38.700 --> 17:42.170
And so he came following you, eh?

17:42.170 --> 17:46.900
But I never would have guessed that
Gouyokuou-san's love interest was Gekka.

17:46.900 --> 17:50.020
Well, that's the story, so...

17:50.020 --> 17:52.420
Please! Allow us to get married!

17:52.420 --> 17:53.690
Father!

17:53.690 --> 17:54.650
Father?!

17:54.650 --> 17:55.670
M-Marry?!

17:55.670 --> 17:57.530
Don't panic, you fool!

17:57.530 --> 17:58.690
B-But!

17:58.690 --> 17:59.560
Anyway!

17:59.560 --> 18:00.440
Hey, Gouyokuou!

18:00.440 --> 18:00.810
Yes!

18:01.080 --> 18:06.400
There is no parent who'd go, "May I take you daughter away?" "Yes, go ahead."

18:06.400 --> 18:10.640
And especially Gekka! She's my daughter who I raised with love!

18:10.640 --> 18:11.830
Was I?

18:12.350 --> 18:13.480
Then what do I do?

18:13.480 --> 18:14.610
This, of course!

18:14.900 --> 18:17.250
If you want to marry Gekka, then get down on your knees!

18:17.250 --> 18:19.320
You must swear your loyalty to your mother! Cry!

18:19.320 --> 18:21.370
Cry and beg for the permission!

18:21.370 --> 18:24.620
I get it. So that's this planet's custom.

18:24.620 --> 18:25.960
Thank you so much for teaching me.

18:26.130 --> 18:29.490
Ouka! If you're the father, then act like one and do your job!

18:29.490 --> 18:30.560
What? My job?

18:30.560 --> 18:33.360
"You need to let me punch you once if you want to marry my daughter", of course!

18:33.360 --> 18:35.590
It's the standard practice in home drama! I've seen it on TV many times!

18:35.590 --> 18:37.430
That's all it takes?

18:37.430 --> 18:38.900
If that's the case, then please go right ahead.

18:38.900 --> 18:40.050
No, even if you insist on...

18:40.050 --> 18:43.030
Please, hit me hard. Don't hesitate and hit me good, Father!

18:43.030 --> 18:45.100
Keep a distance, you fool!

18:45.100 --> 18:47.900
Just listening to you guys embarrasses me.

18:47.900 --> 18:49.810
I do not care for any of these.

18:49.810 --> 18:51.280
What? But...

18:51.280 --> 18:53.510
We'll deal with you later.

18:53.510 --> 18:57.200
There's something I must confirm.

18:57.880 --> 18:59.560
Something you must confirm?

18:59.560 --> 19:02.600
I've come only to discern that.

19:02.600 --> 19:04.870
You should wait here awhile.

19:04.870 --> 19:06.020
Gekka...

19:07.440 --> 19:09.910
Well, if you say so, then we can't do anything about it.

19:09.910 --> 19:13.170
He waited for a thousand years,
so another day or two won't mean a thing.

19:13.170 --> 19:14.940
Now that that's settled, let's go!

19:14.940 --> 19:15.920
Mother?

19:15.920 --> 19:17.540
What? Are you sure?

19:17.540 --> 19:20.020
Shut up. I said it's okay, so it's okay!

19:20.020 --> 19:21.410
You get in, too!

19:23.720 --> 19:24.760
Gekka.

19:24.760 --> 19:26.190
There they go.

19:26.190 --> 19:28.330
And you waited for a thousand years, too.

19:28.330 --> 19:31.730
I feel bad for Gouyokuou-san.

19:33.750 --> 19:36.230
Gekka's so cute after all!

19:38.250 --> 19:39.310
Gekka...

19:42.280 --> 19:47.370
So, what is it that you have to check?

19:49.580 --> 19:50.400
Gekka?

19:50.400 --> 19:52.520
You're as thoughtless as ever!

19:52.520 --> 19:56.790
A father who tries to find out about what his daughter doesn't want to talk about will be hated by her!

19:56.790 --> 19:57.510
But...

19:57.840 --> 20:00.260
Can't you trust your own daughter?

20:00.690 --> 20:02.220
I...

20:06.090 --> 20:07.350
Okay.

20:07.350 --> 20:08.270
But Gekka.

20:08.920 --> 20:12.400
If there is anything we can help you with, let us know.

20:12.570 --> 20:17.230
That's right. As a most wonderful fact,
I, Kyouka-sama, am omniscient and omnipotent!

20:17.920 --> 20:20.240
Father... Mother...

20:28.040 --> 20:29.020
Hyouka?

20:29.020 --> 20:31.330
Oh, Hyouka. I'm surprised you found me here.

20:31.330 --> 20:32.760
Stupid Gekka!

20:33.330 --> 20:34.420
Hyouka?

20:34.710 --> 20:37.040
H-Hyouka...

20:37.040 --> 20:39.300
Hyouka hit me...

20:39.300 --> 20:43.010
Of course I would! Disappearing like that and making me worry!

20:43.010 --> 20:45.790
And why did you do such a mean thing like that to me?!

20:45.790 --> 20:49.270
Well I... have many complicated matters going on.

20:49.270 --> 20:50.440
Where's your "I'm sorry"?!

20:50.440 --> 20:52.790
Say "I'm sorry," you stupid jellyfish!

20:52.790 --> 20:54.690
Calm down a little, Hyouka.

20:54.690 --> 20:57.850
It's not very peaceful to punch your older sister.

20:59.520 --> 21:03.670
But... But Gekka's the bad one!

21:06.130 --> 21:08.480
Say "I'm sorry!"

21:08.830 --> 21:10.290
I'm sorry.

21:15.530 --> 21:18.590
What did you all come here for?

21:19.480 --> 21:24.470
What did you all come to this planet for
after years of travel?

21:24.880 --> 21:25.930
Why?

21:27.600 --> 21:29.720
Must I explain?

21:30.230 --> 21:32.740
Looks like you've already been influenced by this planet.

21:33.070 --> 21:39.260
Look at you, covering yourself with a thin coating and acting like a human on this planet.

21:39.260 --> 21:41.840
So what? Just answer me!

21:42.240 --> 21:45.660
Why should I? You are no longer me.

21:46.660 --> 21:49.100
Farewell, Princess.

22:06.200 --> 22:09.100
You, who are thinking about falling asleep with the remote in hand!

22:09.100 --> 22:12.700
Even if others forgive you, I, Kyouka-sama, won't allow such a godless act!

22:12.700 --> 22:15.800
Sit on the floor, in front of the TV, and start worshipping!

23:25.070 --> 23:26.190
This is Yuuka.

23:26.190 --> 23:28.950
Is Gouyokuou a good person or a bad person? Which is he?

23:28.950 --> 23:30.640
Honored Sister. We have another new character again.

23:31.320 --> 23:32.970
Isn't our screen time becoming less and less?

23:33.150 --> 23:34.640
And it's another female.

23:34.640 --> 23:35.680
Wow.

23:35.680 --> 23:39.010
Next time: Matter X from Space
